<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT CZECH REPUBLIC 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT CZECH REPUBLIC 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>VALLADOLID, Spain 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain beat the Czech</p>
<p>Republic 1-0 (halftime 1-0) in their World Cup European group</p>
<p>six qualifier on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Fernando Hierro 40 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Spain: 1-Andoni Zubizarreta 2-Albert Ferrer 3-Emilio</p>
<p>Amavisca (18-Guillermo Amor 75) 4-Rafael Alkorta 5-Abelardo</p>
<p>Fernandez 6-Fernando Hierro 7-Javier Manjarin (15-Ismael Urzaiz</p>
<p>56) 8-Kiko Narvaez (14-Roberto Rios 84) 9-Josep Guardiola</p>
<p>10-Raul Gonzalez 11-Alfonso Perez</p>
<p>Czech Republic: 1-Pavel Srnicek 2-Radoslav Latal 3-Karel</p>
<p>Rada 4-Pavel Nedved 5-Miroslav Kadlec (17-Karel Poborsky 68)</p>
<p>6-Michal Hornak 7-Jiri Nemec 8-Tomas Repka 9-Martin Cizek</p>
<p>(15-Martin Frydek 69) 10-Vladimir Smicer 11-Rene Wagner</p>
<p>(12-Horst Siegl 73)</p>
<p>    Standings   P  W  D  L   F  A  Pts  </p>
<p> Spain	    8  6  2  0  21   4  20</p>
<p> Yugoslavia     8  6  1  1  23   6  19</p>
<p> Slovakia	 6  4  0  2  14   7  12</p>
<p> Faroe Islands  7  2  0  5   9  24   6</p>
<p> Czech Republic 5  1  1  3   7   4   4</p>
<p> Malta	    8  0  0  8   2  31   0</p>
<p>Next match: Aug 20 - Czech Republic v Faroe Islands</p>
